WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.320
The Three Stooges, Painfully Funny.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:25.860
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.700
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.980
And today we're going to talk about Ghostbusters 2.

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.560
Oh, but not really.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.540
We're in the wrong episode, Sean.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:41.440
Well, let's just start there.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:46.560
I think this is the first time we've seen a fourth wall break in an NES game.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:55.820
Absolutely. And arguably the strongest, not to say that the game sucks or anything, but that is a very strong start for this game.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.840
It's a very Stanley parable.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.620
Yeah. And considering that Ghostbusters 2 hasn't even released yet.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:07.680
So it's like at least a video game, you know, it's like, why would you make that joke?

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.240
Like, I wouldn't think that I was getting Ghostbusters 2 at all.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.800
If anything, they should reference an older game that they already made.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.120
Like Ghostbusters.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.620
You know? Or Defender of the Crown.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:20.020
Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.900
I don't think they made the original Ghostbusters.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.120
The Ghostbusters 2, as far as I know, is not a Ghostbusters franchise simulator.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.380
That's true. I mean, maybe it isn't.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.800
I don't know. Yeah.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:39.980
Now, you know, we have to talk about, so you start the game, Ghostbusters 2 shows up, and then there's some good voice acting, too.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:45.580
Like, you can actually hear, I don't know who's who, Moe, Curly, the other guy.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:46.620
Yeah, the three people.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.240
Who is the third one?

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.360
Moe, Curly? Come on, let's like make people cringe.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.800
It's Jerry, no.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.820
Larry. Larry, Curly, and Moe, yeah.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:13.000
There you go. Yeah, so obviously we have no familiarity with the Three Stooges, but just not even because they're like not from our time or anything, but like I haven't really ever thought that like that kind of like comedy would be appealing to me today.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.460
I don't know.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.680
That's like, that's back when like throwing a pie in someone's face was funny.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.100
That's gone now.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.240
You can't get a laugh.

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:25.100
I think it's probably, it's still funny, but you just have to do it like in the right context.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.000
Like you have to ironically throw it into their face now.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.140
Like it's not just straight up funny.

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:35.180
Or it's got to be like on YouTube with somebody who didn't know that they were going to get pie.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.800
It can't be like in the show.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:47.360
You know, the fact that like a television show would have like, this is like to me, I would think of the Three Stooges as the original impractical jokers, but minus the reality section of it.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:52.000
See, I know of the impractical jokers, but I know nothing about them.

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.100
Are they like lame?

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:54.780
Are they lame? Yeah.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.700
Well, okay. Look, I don't want to upset anybody.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.980
I just don't think they're not the funniest people in the world.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:04.360
They laugh at their own stuff more than it's probably been laughed at.

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:09.620
I mean, that's probably going to upset some people, but I get what you're saying.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:18.280
Now, the Three Stooges video game, I don't think it's weird to say, but this is strange in 1989.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:29.600
We've talked about some games, some questionable movies that then get like, you know, an NES port and it's like, all right, that's a little strange for the audience, but whatever.

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.340
This time, it's actually strange, right?

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:45.060
The Three Stooges, the guys from like the 30s and 40s now are getting a NES video game where you basically do like a bunch of different mini games.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.580
It's Mario Party.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.680
I was thinking it's even like WarioWare.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.680
Yeah, WarioWare, Mario Party, Three Stooges.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:04:02.840
But like, just going back to what you were saying, like, is there any, to our knowledge, any cultural relevance to this game being released now, like 1989?

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:05.700
Like, is there a re-release or something?

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:06.500
Do we know?

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:16.600
To the best of my abilities, all I can tell is that the Three Stooges was still running in syndication in the 80s.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.820
Okay. That makes sense, I guess.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:24.760
There was no movie, but this also wasn't like the first version of this game.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:32.700
The NES one is a port of, I forget which computer, but one of those, like either the Apple II or...

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.400
Amiga. Yeah, the Amiga or something.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:36.520
It's a port of this to the NES.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.860
And this is a game that will only become more confounding.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.840
I'm not going to do the sequels and spinoffs now, but just a tease for later in the episode.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:54.460
You won't believe the kind of legs that the Three Stooges, this exact game with no added bonuses or remastering, you won't believe what legs it has in terms of ports.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:55.720
So stick around for that.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.560
But in the meantime, let's talk about the actual game.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:09.140
The Three Stooges, it's essentially like setting up what I would think would be the stronger thing to do is set up like an episode of the Three Stooges and then you like go through it.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:22.360
But instead, they have to rescue an orphanage by earning enough money in mini games that are based on various Three Stooges films or TV episodes or what have you.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:31.860
I just feel like that's a little complicated because there's the whole somebody is trying to steal the orphanage first, right?

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.280
Like this Mr. Money guy.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.380
Oh, yeah.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:37.820
Yeah, he's got the keys to the orphanage.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:41.800
So you have to earn enough money to buy it back from him as if he would.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.840
He wasn't just doing it for nefarious purposes.

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:45.880
He's just doing it for money accumulation.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.580
I thought it was just rent. Like they just need to pay rent that month.

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.440
But it's not even their orphanage.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:59.140
It's like some. Yeah, like, you know, but like they're just like, oh, we're going to take up the cause of this orphanage and their late rent.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:00.880
I got it. Okay.

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.940
That's just something that the Three Stooges do.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:08.300
So you hope that like in your own hometown, you run into them and be like, hey, could you pay my rent this month?

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.240
Well, I mean, if you have orphans in your house, maybe they will.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.200
But what was so?

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.980
Okay. Then you get into this other thing where they sort of congregate on against a brick wall.

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:26.040
And now they're going to select the jobs they're going to do that day.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:30.280
And I don't know what was what were your thoughts on this?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:40.780
Right. So this is the this is how they gamify it then, because now you only have 30 in game days to earn enough money to get the orphanage back.

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:44.420
So the jobs that they take are the minigames.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:46.300
That's where it gets clever again.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.800
Now I'm like, oh, I understand what the assignment is.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.580
And the the the jobs being the minigames.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:54.600
Yes, it's it's Mario Party.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.040
It's WarioWare.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:02.680
These are short bursts of gameplay that I'm not sure if I fully understood all of them.

00:07:02.680 --> 00:07:06.240
But at least they didn't at least they didn't last forever.

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.820
And at least you got to like, you know, you got to like experience some really weird stuff.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:17.800
I feel like at, you know, at this point, we could just talk about every single one of them.

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:22.780
But for me, in terms of standout minigames, that soup cracker one.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.680
Oh, okay. It's just it's just wild.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:28.580
Okay, I get that this is a reference to an episode.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:34.680
And maybe some of our listeners are big Three Stooges fans and they get what's happening, what happens in that episode.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.160
But I have zero context.

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:37.460
But all right.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:43.640
So one of them is they're there for for eating soup really fast.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:46.700
And there's clams in the soup and there's crackers that they want.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.380
And you have to get all the crackers.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:53.740
But then the clams will close on a cracker, sometimes uneventfully.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:08:03.880
But other times we'll get this ear piercing screech of what I imagine is the Stooges in question shrieking in horror from a clam eating his cracker.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:07.120
But I can't really tell because I didn't really know what triggered it.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.880
Do you know what's going on here?

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.360
Yes. So the Stooges in question is curly.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:17.040
I don't know why he's wearing that hat because he wasn't wearing it a minute ago.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:23.880
But now he's wearing a hat and he's got a bottle of wine, which is also questionable because like, I don't know.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:27.040
Do you ever have like wine with your other liquids?

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:28.640
No, no, no. That's olive oil.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:30.080
Oh, wait.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.240
I don't know. For the soup? Yeah.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:38.800
Anyway, I guess like olive oil is less objectionable, I suppose, because at least that would like be infusing another taste.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.520
Whereas maybe I can't imagine like I'll have the lobster bisque and a glass of red.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:44.700
Like it just doesn't happen.

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.260
You know, you're drinking one thing.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:53.920
Stick to one. Nobody says, can I have, you know, a bottle of red and a bottle of cool blue Gatorade?

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.320
I mean, don't knock it till you try it.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.320
That's true. So, yes, what's happening here, Sean, is exactly what you think is happening.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:07.060
The first off, kudos to the sprite work here, because that's a pretty good image of curly.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:21.340
But then even the over, you know, the top down view of the hand with the spoon trying to like be, you know, hovering over the soup and trying to get the crackers before the clams eat them all up.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.820
That is a very easily understood assignment.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.980
This is where I think about like WarioWare, right?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:32.820
Where in a WarioWare game, you only have like 10 seconds of actual gameplay anyway, and they don't tell you what to do.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:33.800
It just comes across the screen.

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.800
It's like jump. And then you just like, OK, I guess I'm jumping.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:43.340
And then you as you play it over time, you figure out like what you actually like need to do and get used to the rhythm.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:45.640
And the game gets faster and faster here.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:47.120
It was like right away. I was like, I get it.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:48.640
I'm supposed to be eating these crackers.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:53.880
If the clams get to them first, Curly's just pissed.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:10:01.680
And yeah, he shrieks the loudest, maybe the maybe the noisiest audio file I've ever heard on the NES yet.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:09.000
And it's not pleasant, but also it's unclear about like the timing of how long it takes a clam to get a cracker.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:11.200
And it's not every cracker.

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:15.060
It's not every cracker that is then eaten by a clam.

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:24.280
I don't know if it's just the first cracker that gets eaten by a clam in each bowl or if there's just a random time that like you're never going to get that cracker.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:30.460
Because then there'll be a bunch of times where the clams close on the cracker and nothing happens.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:34.860
I don't get that little screen that little FMV.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:47.080
Yeah. And I mean, we see we see some stuff in terms of just confusing sprite work and and very pixelated images of the Stooges featured throughout other mini games, too.

00:10:47.320 --> 00:11:00.200
There's that one where you're like simultaneously boxing and trying to dodge obstacles and look at a stopwatch that that one has like a very like Tim and Eric picture of of I think Moe.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:04.840
You know, it's it's all like the visuals are whatever for me.

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:09.480
I'd rather, you know, stick on the on the mini game thing for a moment just because.

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:30.720
Like a lot of these games created for me the Mario Party effect where if you're not in the mini game mode of Mario Party and selecting the mini games you want to play, if you're actually on the board, there's that time where like after everybody's gone for their turn, the wheel comes down and you just pray that like that one game doesn't get picked.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.060
You know, like that.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:34.780
And it does. And it's it's the trivia.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:38.400
And it's not because I don't know the three Stooges like, yeah, that sucks.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:44.900
But like in general, trivia for the three Stooges implies that like in this game, at least.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.000
Right. Only super fans should be owning a copy of the three Stooges.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:55.000
Like there's no accessibility here for newcoming fans or people who are just interested in these three weird characters.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:59.500
It's like, no, now you won't earn a penny because you don't know anything about the show.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:03.580
And thankfully, there's only three possible solutions.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:07.840
So like you're bound to get some money from this if you just randomly select.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:10.220
But that's not how you want to play this game.

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:20.060
Like you. But the questions that are asked are like, in what year did Curly join the show played by whoever the hell?

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:23.140
And it's like 1936 or 1942.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.440
Like, I don't know.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:28.520
And I guess it's just the less the least fun part of the game.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.940
Yeah, you brought up a great point there, Sean, though.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.180
The trivia isn't like.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.140
All right, so I'm going to change it to something I know.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.500
Right. So Simpsons trivia.

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:46.220
Right. If you ask me about something that happened in an episode of The Simpsons, I might be able to like answer a lot of those potential questions.

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:50.420
But if you start saying like, who was the executive producer of season 12?

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:53.900
Right. It's like, oh, I might know, but I wouldn't.

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.440
I'm a super fan here.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:13:02.780
It's like the three stooges questions aren't always about just like the pranks that they pulled on each other or like famous catchphrases.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:07.240
It's like actual actors names or celebrities who appeared on the show.

00:13:07.240 --> 00:13:09.200
And that just makes it all the more confusing.

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:13.000
Yeah, I don't truly get like.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:23.960
I think if you chose any like piece of fandom, that's that's just that's not the kind of trivia you're going to ask.

00:13:23.960 --> 00:13:36.780
It's just it's yeah, it's very strange that it's more like making of stuff or maybe the fans of this show are disproportionately knowledgeable about the making of the three stooges.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:14:00.640
There's another minigame where you're at like a fancy dinner banquet.

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:09.360
And you have to throw pies in the faces of the more regal looking guests.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:11.280
And they are the hoity toity club.

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:12.700
Oh, there you go.

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:19.820
And they will throw pies back at you and you're trying to hit them with pies to earn money.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:21.160
So, again, unclear.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:28.980
But then again, I also I don't think like, you know, technically the more soup Curly ate, the less the more money would have cost him to eat the soup.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:34.740
So, you know, by that logic, you shouldn't have earned any money for eating crackers.

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:39.620
I don't think he was just going to like a restaurant ordering of all these soups.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:43.800
I think he was a part of like a competition, like a soup eating competition.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:46.520
Oh, OK. So this is a pie throwing competition.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:48.020
No, no, no. You're a waiter.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:53.420
You're supposed to be serving pies to these people and you don't get paid if you drop pies.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.100
Got it. OK, it's all making sense now.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.180
Thank you so much for explaining it to me and the listeners.

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:11.800
Absolutely. I found the control scheme of this one to be something that made me say, please don't ever pick this one again because you don't have a clear like.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:19.480
So the three are, you know, just like in a row, but you control all three of them at once.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:25.420
And there's different inputs for like who's going to pick up the pie versus who's going to throw the pie.

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:29.820
And when the other people are ducking, you have to like look out for that.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:42.460
It had that whole, you know, we've used this before, that quop thing going on where it just felt unintuitive because it's not how I would actually think about targeting people with pies in a two dimensional video game.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:46.860
Instead, they just created their own rules about what buttons you might have to press.

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:49.840
I actually found it relatively intuitive.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:57.740
Like basically they're lined up in a row, like going into the depth of the frame and.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:11.100
Um, to select who on your team, who of the stooges is going to duck up is for the farthest back, left or right is for the middle guy.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:15.560
And, uh, down is for the one closest to you.

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:22.920
And so like, you know, when you're viewing the guys from these angles, from this angle, it kind of like lines up with the D pad.

00:16:23.060 --> 00:16:28.220
But then when you want to throw, it adds a button you have to hold and then you're pressing the same button again.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:34.840
So it's, it's elegant in one way and then really fumbly in another.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:38.320
So I get what you're saying, but I also kind of got what they were trying to do.

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:50.940
Then you have, you know, on the wheel, you have a bunch of other mini games and stuff too, but you also have some weird things like mousetraps that just immediately are like that.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.120
That's it's not a game over necessarily.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:57.160
I think you need to, uh, how many mousetraps is it?

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.680
Four? It's either four or five where you like, oh, game over.

00:17:00.820 --> 00:17:02.040
You ran out of fingers or something.

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:07.000
Yeah. They injure the finger, um, of one of the stooges.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:13.100
And then once they have, uh, four, five would make more sense, I suppose, but there's nothing you can do with just a thumb.

00:17:13.620 --> 00:17:20.600
So, uh, what, you know, once you've lost four fingers, it immediately ends the game regardless of the numbers of days completed.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.040
Dude, does it really need that?

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:30.140
Do we really need like a, um, this is like similar to wheel of fortune with the bankrupt, uh, thing on the wheel.

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:33.640
It's like, there's already other ways to lose money in these games.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:36.500
Do we really need one that just stops the game for you?

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:42.980
Yeah, because there's, I think there's only one other, um, tile that loses you money.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:53.180
